<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Makhado</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1895</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Makhado Ramabulana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Makhado was a king of the Venda in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soutpansberg">Soutpansberg</a> region of what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, from 1864 until his death in 1895. He led Venda resistance against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boers</a> of the Zoutpansberg, whose attacks in 1867 forced them to abandon the settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schoemansdal">Schoemansdal</a>. The town of Louis Trichardt was renamed Makhado in his honour in 2003.</p></div>
